From fff4b2f48e952e9c59955a8f4aa61aeee360d299 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:42:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(deepseek-v4.1): sequence-parallel prefill wherever it
 can pay

Drop SPARK3_DS41_PREFILL_SP_MIN_ROWS. SP trades two all-gathers per layer
for reduce-scatters that split the row-wise work across the ranks, so the
threshold follows from that trade instead of a setting. A forward runs
sequence-parallel when it is prompt processing (larger than the largest
CUDA graph capture size and max_num_seqs * (1 + k)) and its padded
hidden-state message exceeds what the one-shot RoCE all-reduce takes:
below that the all-reduce costs the same as the full-row path, the
row-wise kernels are latency-bound, and SP only adds the gathers
(+6 ms of all-gathers against 1 ms of mHC savings on a 60-token prompt).
With the 2 MiB RoCE limit and 5120 bf16 hidden rows that is 205 tokens
at TP 3, where the previous 2048-token cut left 4-6% on 1-2K prompts.

The RoCE communicator exposes its limit as all_reduce_max_bytes.
